---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/pages/ai.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="AI — a_e.s_" description="One place for AGI tracking, wave analysis, environmental impact, post-labor economics, and civic AI accountability." theme="archive">


  <section class="ai-hub-hero">
    <p class="ai-hub-kicker">AI Area</p>
    <h1>AI, Automation &amp; Accountability</h1>
    <p>One place for tracking AGI development, wave-by-wave disruption analysis, the environmental cost of AI, post-labor economic models, and what accountability looks like in practice.</p>
  </section>

  <nav class="ai-subnav" aria-label="AI section navigation">
    <a href="/agi">AGI Monitor</a>
    <a href="/ai-waves">AI Waves</a>
    <a href="/environmental-weight-of-ai">Environmental Weight</a>
    <a href="/post-labor-economics">Post-Labor Economics</a>
    <a href="/ai-accountability-pledge">Accountability Pledge</a>
    <a href="#theory">Theory &amp; Reference</a>
  </nav>

  <div class="ai-section-grid">
    <a class="ai-card" href="/agi">
      <span class="ai-card-tag">Monitor</span>
      <h2>AGI Timeline</h2>
      <p>A tracked, phase-structured timeline of AI signals, benchmarks, and labor-displacement events across the agentic stumble, infrastructure convergence, and moment-of-truth windows.</p>
      <span class="ai-card-link">Open timeline →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="ai-card" href="/ai-waves">
      <span class="ai-card-tag">Analysis</span>
      <h2>AI Waves</h2>
      <p>Four-wave disruption model covering software automation, hardware convergence, societal integration, and post-scarcity transition. The right frame is utility and labor effect, not a ceremonial AGI day.</p>
      <span class="ai-card-link">Read the model →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="ai-card" href="/environmental-weight-of-ai">
      <span class="ai-card-tag">Environmental</span>
      <h2>Environmental Weight of AI</h2>
      <p>Carbon footprint, water consumption, and energy cost of training and running large AI models — with real comparison benchmarks and the silver linings worth tracking.</p>
      <span class="ai-card-link">View data →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="ai-card" href="/post-labor-economics">
      <span class="ai-card-tag">Economics</span>
      <h2>Post-Labor Economics</h2>
      <p>A systems model of the demand crisis: automation raises productive capacity while shrinking wage-based distribution, pushing toward new forms of economic agency beyond employment alone.</p>
      <span class="ai-card-link">View model →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="ai-card" href="/ai-accountability-pledge">
      <span class="ai-card-tag">Civic</span>
      <h2>AI Accountability Pledge</h2>
      <p>The commitment — civic and measurable — to transparent, accountable AI use in creative and community work.</p>
      <span class="ai-card-link">Read the pledge →</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <section class="ai-waves-section" id="waves">
    <h2>AI Waves — Disruption Model</h2>
    <p>The right frame for the current moment is utility and labor effect, not waiting for a ceremonial AGI day.</p>
    <div class="ai-waves-grid">
      <div class="ai-wave-item">
        <h3>Wave 1 — Software</h3>
        <p class="wave-years">2024–2027 · Active</p>
        <p>Routine knowledge work automation. Deployment economics drive adoption more than raw capability. Partial automation before dependable autonomy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ai-wave-item">
        <h3>Wave 2 — Hardware</h3>
        <p class="wave-years">2026–2030 · Emerging</p>
        <p>Robotics and physical automation reach economic viability at scale. Hardware costs cross the labor-cost threshold.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ai-wave-item">
        <h3>Wave 3 — Integration</h3>
        <p class="wave-years">2029–2033 · Forecast</p>
        <p>AI systems coordinate with each other and with infrastructure. Energy and compute supply chains become the primary pace-setter.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ai-wave-item">
        <h3>Wave 4 — Transition</h3>
        <p class="wave-years">2032–? · Speculative</p>
        <p>Post-scarcity economic pressure intensifies. The question shifts to what ownership structures replace wage-based distribution.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ai-theory-section" id="theory">
    <h2>Theory &amp; Reference</h2>
    <p>Key video references that shaped the AGI framing and post-labor model used across this section.</p>
    <div class="ai-theory-links">
      <a class="ai-theory-link" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QvFoRk4JsPc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <span class="ai-theory-link-icon">▶</span>
        <div class="ai-theory-link-text">
          <strong>AGI Theory — Reference Talk</strong>
          <span>youtube.com · Key framing for the four-wave disruption timeline</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a class="ai-theory-link" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4rzeW4dbvlQ&t=1s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <span class="ai-theory-link-icon">▶</span>
        <div class="ai-theory-link-text">
          <strong>OpenAI Farming — Labor Displacement Model</strong>
          <span>youtube.com · On the economics of AI-driven labor reshaping</span>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
